	abstract = {View recent discussion. Abstract: Chains-of-thought (CoT) allow language models to verbalise multi-step rationales before producing their final answer. While this technique often boosts task performance and offers an impression of transparency into the model’s reasoning, we argue that CoT rationales can be misleading and are neither necessary nor sufficient for trustworthy interpretability.},
